{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "fa49bd57-3cd6-8d60-a0d9-4b22cc126513",
  "created_at": "2025-12-15T16:00:52-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Joao Resendes",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:58:54-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:58:57-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hey Tony, Joao Resendes here. So I'm going to apologize in advance, I'm the guy who opens the bill and then stares at it like it's a crossword."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:06-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're not the first. What's it say?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:09-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, it covers a whole quarter. Three months. I don't get a bill every month like the electric, so why a quarter? And how do you count the dates? Mine starts mid-September and ends mid-December, which isn't even a real quarter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:22-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, so we read meters on a cycle, not on the calendar. Each route gets read about every three months, so your dates follow when the reader got to your street, not January, April, and so on. Could be a day or two different each time."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so the dates float. Fine. Then there's this line that says consumption. Consumption of what? I'm not eating the water."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:43-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Ha. Consumption just means how much water you used in that period. The meter reading at the end minus the reading at the start. The sewer part is usually figured off that same number."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T15:59:54-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. So it's just the usage. Wish they'd just say usage. Seems like a lot for the two of us, but whatever, I'm not going to fight a meter on a Monday."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:05-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "If you think the reading's off, I can note it and we can have it rechecked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:11-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Let me look at it first. Different question. I get home after you folks close. Is there a drop box at City Hall where I can drop a check after closing time?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:21-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there's a payment drop box at City Hall. Put the check in an envelope with the stub or your account number on it and it gets picked up the next business day."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:32-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Perfect. And, hey, I'm at 121 Dixon Street, North End. Can see the lighthouse from my kitchen window, so at least the water bill comes with a view."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:41-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that's a nice perk. Anything else I can do for you today, Joao?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:46-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nope, that's it. Thanks, Tony."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2025-12-15T16:00:49-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Take care. Have a good evening."
    }
  ],
